a. Explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":" takes precedence when it is non-empty."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"highlightedcodefence","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HighlightedCodeFence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"core#renderedcodeblockdata","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RenderedCodeBlockData"}]},{"type":"text","value":" plus the resolved "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decorations"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rendercodefence","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderCodeFence"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function renderCodeFence(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HighlightedCodeFence","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses inline diff notation and metadata, then delegates to the supplied highlighter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hast","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HAST"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hasttext","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HastText"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A HAST-compatible text node with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'text'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hastelement","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HastElement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A HAST-compatible element node with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tagName"},{"type":"text","value":", optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"properties"},{"type":"text","value":", and recursive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"codefencetohast","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeFenceToHast"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function codeFenceToHast(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HastElement","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<pre class=\"th-code th-code--LANG\"><code>...</code></pre>"},{"type":"text","value":" HAST tree. A title is exposed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dataTitle"},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pre"},{"type":"text","value":" node."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tokenstohast","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tokensToHast"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function tokensToHast(\n  tokens: ReadonlyArray<HighlightToken>,\n  lang: string,\n  options?: {\n    decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n    lineNumbers?: boolean\n    title?: string\n  },\n): HastElement","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders existing tokens to the same HAST structure without tokenizing code."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"markdown-api","text":"Markdown API","level":1},{"id":"tanstack-markdown-adapter","text":"TanStack Markdown adapter","level":2},{"id":"tanstackmarkdownhighlighteroptions","text":"TanStackMarkdownHighlighterOptions","level":3},{"id":"tanstackmarkdownhighlighter","text":"TanStackMarkdownHighlighter","level":3},{"id":"createtanstackmarkdownhighlighter","text":"createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter","level":3},{"id":"metadata","text":"Metadata","level":2},{"id":"parsecodediffnotation","text":"parseCodeDiffNotation","level":3},{"id":"codefencemeta","text":"CodeFenceMeta","level":3},{"id":"parsecodefencemeta","text":"parseCodeFenceMeta","level":3},{"id":"getcodefencetitle","text":"getCodeFenceTitle","level":3},{"id":"fence-rendering","text":"Fence rendering","level":2},{"id":"codefenceinput","text":"CodeFenceInput","level":3},{"id":"highlightedcodefence","text":"HighlightedCodeFence","level":3},{"id":"rendercodefence","text":"renderCodeFence","level":3},{"id":"hast","text":"HAST","level":2},{"id":"hasttext","text":"HastText","level":3},{"id":"hastelement","text":"HastElement","level":3},{"id":"codefencetohast","text":"codeFenceToHast","level":3},{"id":"tokenstohast","text":"tokensToHast","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Markdown API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/markdown` converts Markdown code-fence inputs into rendered block data or HAST. It does not parse Markdown documents.\n\n## TanStack Markdown adapter\n\n### `TanStackMarkdownHighlighterOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype TanStackMarkdownHighlighterOptions = {\n  highlightLines?: ReadonlyArray<number>\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n### `TanStackMarkdownHighlighter`\n\nA synchronous callback matching TanStack Markdown's code-highlighter contract without importing `@tanstack/markdown`.\n\n### `createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter`\n\n```ts\nfunction createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter(\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): TanStackMarkdownHighlighter\n```\n\nReturns escaped inner token markup for a renderer-owned `<code>` element. Highlighted lines receive `th-line--highlighted`; unknown languages use the highlighter's configured fallback.\n\n## Metadata\n\n### `parseCodeDiffNotation`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCodeDiffNotation(code: string): {\n  code: string\n  decorations: Array<HighlightDecoration>\n}\n```\n\nRemoves trailing `[!code ++]` and `[!code --]` directives and returns `th-line--inserted` and `th-line--deleted` decorations for their one-based line numbers. JavaScript-style line and block comments, `#` line comments, and HTML comments are supported.\n\nBoth LF and Windows CRLF line endings are preserved when directives are removed.\n\n### `CodeFenceMeta`\n\n```ts\ntype CodeFenceMeta = {\n  decorations: Array<HighlightDecoration>\n  lineNumbers: boolean\n  title?: string\n}\n```\n\n### `parseCodeFenceMeta`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCodeFenceMeta(meta?: string | null): CodeFenceMeta\n```\n\nRecognizes `title`, `filename`, `file`, `name`, `lineNumbers`, `showLineNumbers`, shorthand highlighted lines, and named line annotations. Invalid line fragments are ignored. See [Annotations](../guides/annotations).\n\nQuoted values are treated as text, so `title=\"lineNumbers {2}\"` sets a title without enabling line numbers or highlighting a line. Named annotations require braces, for example `ins={2}`, and line numbers must be positive safe integers with ascending ranges.\n\n### `getCodeFenceTitle`\n\n```ts\nfunction getCodeFenceTitle(meta?: string | null): string | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the trimmed value of the first `title`, `filename`, `file`, or `name` assignment. Single-quoted, double-quoted, and unquoted values are accepted.\n\n## Fence rendering\n\n### `CodeFenceInput`\n\n```ts\ntype CodeFenceInput = {\n  code: string\n  decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n  lang?: string | null\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  meta?: string | null\n  title?: string | null\n}\n```\n\nInline diff notation is converted first, followed by metadata and explicit `decorations`. Explicit `lineNumbers` takes precedence over metadata. Explicit `title` takes precedence when it is non-empty.\n\n### `HighlightedCodeFence`\n\n[`RenderedCodeBlockData`](core#renderedcodeblockdata) plus the resolved `decorations` and `lineNumbers`.\n\n### `renderCodeFence`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderCodeFence(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HighlightedCodeFence\n```\n\nParses inline diff notation and metadata, then delegates to the supplied highlighter.\n\n## HAST\n\n### `HastText`\n\nA HAST-compatible text node with `type: 'text'` and `value`.\n\n### `HastElement`\n\nA HAST-compatible element node with `type`, `tagName`, optional `properties`, and recursive `children`.\n\n### `codeFenceToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction codeFenceToHast(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HastElement\n```\n\nReturns a `<pre class=\"th-code th-code--LANG\"><code>...</code></pre>` HAST tree. A title is exposed as `dataTitle` on the `pre` node.\n\n### `tokensToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction tokensToHast(\n  tokens: ReadonlyArray<HighlightToken>,\n  lang: string,\n  options?: {\n    decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n    lineNumbers?: boolean\n    title?: string\n  },\n): HastElement\n```\n\nRenders existing tokens to the same HAST structure without tokenizing code.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Markdown API\n---\n\n# Markdown API\n\n`@tanstack/highlight/markdown` converts Markdown code-fence inputs into rendered block data or HAST. It does not parse Markdown documents.\n\n## TanStack Markdown adapter\n\n### `TanStackMarkdownHighlighterOptions`\n\n```ts\ntype TanStackMarkdownHighlighterOptions = {\n  highlightLines?: ReadonlyArray<number>\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n### `TanStackMarkdownHighlighter`\n\nA synchronous callback matching TanStack Markdown's code-highlighter contract without importing `@tanstack/markdown`.\n\n### `createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter`\n\n```ts\nfunction createTanStackMarkdownHighlighter(\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): TanStackMarkdownHighlighter\n```\n\nReturns escaped inner token markup for a renderer-owned `<code>` element. Highlighted lines receive `th-line--highlighted`; unknown languages use the highlighter's configured fallback.\n\n## Metadata\n\n### `parseCodeDiffNotation`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCodeDiffNotation(code: string): {\n  code: string\n  decorations: Array<HighlightDecoration>\n}\n```\n\nRemoves trailing `[!code ++]` and `[!code --]` directives and returns `th-line--inserted` and `th-line--deleted` decorations for their one-based line numbers. JavaScript-style line and block comments, `#` line comments, and HTML comments are supported.\n\nBoth LF and Windows CRLF line endings are preserved when directives are removed.\n\n### `CodeFenceMeta`\n\n```ts\ntype CodeFenceMeta = {\n  decorations: Array<HighlightDecoration>\n  lineNumbers: boolean\n  title?: string\n}\n```\n\n### `parseCodeFenceMeta`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCodeFenceMeta(meta?: string | null): CodeFenceMeta\n```\n\nRecognizes `title`, `filename`, `file`, `name`, `lineNumbers`, `showLineNumbers`, shorthand highlighted lines, and named line annotations. Invalid line fragments are ignored. See [Annotations](../guides/annotations).\n\nQuoted values are treated as text, so `title=\"lineNumbers {2}\"` sets a title without enabling line numbers or highlighting a line. Named annotations require braces, for example `ins={2}`, and line numbers must be positive safe integers with ascending ranges.\n\n### `getCodeFenceTitle`\n\n```ts\nfunction getCodeFenceTitle(meta?: string | null): string | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the trimmed value of the first `title`, `filename`, `file`, or `name` assignment. Single-quoted, double-quoted, and unquoted values are accepted.\n\n## Fence rendering\n\n### `CodeFenceInput`\n\n```ts\ntype CodeFenceInput = {\n  code: string\n  decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n  lang?: string | null\n  lineNumbers?: boolean\n  meta?: string | null\n  title?: string | null\n}\n```\n\nInline diff notation is converted first, followed by metadata and explicit `decorations`. Explicit `lineNumbers` takes precedence over metadata. Explicit `title` takes precedence when it is non-empty.\n\n### `HighlightedCodeFence`\n\n[`RenderedCodeBlockData`](core#renderedcodeblockdata) plus the resolved `decorations` and `lineNumbers`.\n\n### `renderCodeFence`\n\n```ts\nfunction renderCodeFence(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HighlightedCodeFence\n```\n\nParses inline diff notation and metadata, then delegates to the supplied highlighter.\n\n## HAST\n\n### `HastText`\n\nA HAST-compatible text node with `type: 'text'` and `value`.\n\n### `HastElement`\n\nA HAST-compatible element node with `type`, `tagName`, optional `properties`, and recursive `children`.\n\n### `codeFenceToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction codeFenceToHast(\n  input: CodeFenceInput,\n  highlighter: Highlighter,\n): HastElement\n```\n\nReturns a `<pre class=\"th-code th-code--LANG\"><code>...</code></pre>` HAST tree. A title is exposed as `dataTitle` on the `pre` node.\n\n### `tokensToHast`\n\n```ts\nfunction tokensToHast(\n  tokens: ReadonlyArray<HighlightToken>,\n  lang: string,\n  options?: {\n    decorations?: ReadonlyArray<HighlightDecoration>\n    lineNumbers?: boolean\n    title?: string\n  },\n): HastElement\n```\n\nRenders existing tokens to the same HAST structure without tokenizing code.\n"}
